## B) Attribute extraction  (be evidence-based about it)
================================================================================

Make extraction strategy choices based on measured performance AND cost
($ on LLM use). Stripping redundant text, fewer/shorter prompts, combined calls
are all levers to evaluate — not assume.

SUBJECT ATTRIBUTION BUG — Strength & Authenticity (open, hits the live site).
An MP describing an OPPONENT's broken promise / hypocrisy gets that low score
filed under themselves, so we penalise MPs for doing scrutiny. 37% of low-score
Authenticity examples and 7% of low-score Strength ones; opposition MPs flagged
~4x as often as government MPs (9.8% vs 2.4% on Authenticity). Full write-up,
numbers and root cause: attribute-extraction/EVALUATION.md "Known defect:
subject attribution". Ordered fix:
- [ ] Post-hoc filter in the builder (repairs the live site, no re-scoring):
      drop examples whose judgement subject isn't the speaker. Regex triage now,
      or a cheap Haiku pass over the ~8k Strength/Authenticity explanations.
- [ ] Prompt fixes (cheap, needed regardless): delete strength.txt's "year after
      year they promised to fix the hospital" few-shot (it teaches the bug);
      change authenticity.txt's "signal about that opponent" note to "skip it —
      do not score"; add "only score when the subject is the speaker, their own
      party, or their own government" to both.
- [ ] Add `subject: speaker|other|unclear` to the extraction schema and keep only
      `speaker` at build time. This is the real fix — and `subject: other` is
      exactly the field the PITCH.md claims ledger needs, so nothing is wasted.
- [ ] Until fixed: mark Strength + Authenticity as low-confidence on the site.

EVIDENCE-BASED STRENGTH & AUTHENTICITY (v3.0) — FULL PLAN: see V3_PLAN.md
(root). Ground both attributes in the voting/legislative record instead of
asking the LLM to guess, add `subject` to every scored statement, and make
